{"id": 26578, "group": "gullak-money-oa", "sent_at": "2026-11-12T09:18:28.690437+00:00", "text": "Given an array of size n (10^5),telling the scores of n people before the final race ,\nNow in the final race the person who comes first is given n points,second is given n-1 and so on where the person in the last place is given 1 point.(There cannot be a tie). After the final race, all the players with highest score are given trophy.\nFrom this we need to tell the number of people who have the chances of winning the trophy. for example if n=5, points=[12,14,14,15,15]. output = 4, since player 1 cannot win the trophy even if he wins the race, max points he will score is 12+5 = 17, but highest score in that race would be atleast 18.", "author_tag": "IITR", "reply_to": {"id": 26576, "text": "nobroker sde OA ques ??", "author_tag": "IITM"}, "attachment": null, "deleted": false}
